NUM-13: convert the seepage bottom area of non-tabular storage shapes

exfil_initState() converted the bottom and bank areas of a TABULAR storage
unit from user units to ft2, but set the bottom area of FUNCTIONAL,
CYLINDRICAL, CONICAL and PYRAMIDAL units straight from their coefficients,
which are kept in user units. Under SI a bottom of 100 m2 was used as
100 ft2 (10.8 times too small) and the rest of the surface area was
treated as bank. With Green-Ampt seepage the bank sees half the head, so a
vertical-walled 100 m2 basin lost 21 percent less water than the same basin
described as TABULAR or in US units. Divide the bottom area by
UCF(LENGTH)^2 as the TABULAR case does. US models are unchanged.
The stale "PARITY QUIRK" comment in ExfilSolver::init() is updated.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-13_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/Exfiltration.cpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/Exfiltration.cpp
index a626482..d5d234e 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydraulics/Exfiltration.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydraulics/Exfiltration.cpp
@@ -171,11 +171,8 @@ void ExfilSolver::init(SimulationContext& ctx) {
             //     Legacy: exfil_initState() FUNCTIONAL case (exfil.c:134-141)
             //     Bottom area: at depth=0, area = A*0^B + C = C
             //     Exception: if B==0 (exponent is zero), area = A*1 + C = A+C
-            //     PARITY QUIRK: legacy does NOT unit-convert the FUNCTIONAL
-            //     bottom area (its /UCF at exfil.c:126-129 is inside the
-            //     TABULAR case only), so the raw USER-unit coefficients are
-            //     used directly — storage coefficients stay user-unit
-            //     end-to-end (see PostParseResolver), matching this quirk.
+            //     Storage coefficients stay in USER units end-to-end (see
+            //     PostParseResolver), so the bottom area is converted below.
             double a_coeff = (sr >= 0) ? ctx.node_subtypes.storages.a[static_cast<size_t>(sr)] : 0.0;
             double b_coeff = (sr >= 0) ? ctx.node_subtypes.storages.b[static_cast<size_t>(sr)] : 0.0;
             double c_coeff = (sr >= 0) ? ctx.node_subtypes.storages.c[static_cast<size_t>(sr)] : 0.0;
@@ -197,7 +194,8 @@ void ExfilSolver::init(SimulationContext& ctx) {
             } else if (b_coeff == 0.0) {
                 btm += a_coeff;
             }
-            soa_.btm_area[uk] = btm;
+            const double ucf_len = ucf::UCF(ucf::LENGTH, ctx.options);
+            soa_.btm_area[uk] = btm / (ucf_len * ucf_len);
 
             // For functional/cylindrical/conical/pyramidal shapes,
             // bank seepage extends from depth 0 to infinity (BIG)
